  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Charles Sturt University (CSU) was established in 1989 and has since grown into Australia’s largest regional university. Named after the explorer Captain Charles Napier Sturt, the university is a public institution with a strong commitment to regional Australia and a global reputation for high-quality research and teaching.</p><p>You’ll find that CSU is a leader in online education and holds the distinction of being Australia's first carbon-neutral university. The university offers a diverse range of programmes across several faculties, including: Agriculture and Environment, Arts and Communication, Business, Education and Teaching, Information and Library Studies, Policing, Law, and Security, Science and Engineering, Theology and Islamic Studies</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>At Charles Sturt University, you’ll experience a welcoming and inclusive campus culture. Whether you’re studying at a regional hub or a metropolitan campus, there are over 80 academic and social clubs to help you connect with like-minded peers.</p><p>The university provides extensive support services tailored for you, including:</p><ul><li><strong>International Student Support</strong>: Guidance to help you settle into your first session.</li><li><strong>Wellness Services</strong>: Access to qualified counsellors and a dedicated chaplaincy service.</li><li><strong>Careers and Skills Hub</strong>: Resources to build your network and prepare you for the global job market.</li><li><strong>Diversity Networks</strong>: Inclusive environments for First Nations students and the LGBTIQA+ community.</li></ul>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>You have the opportunity to live right in the heart of the university community. Charles Sturt offers on-campus accommodation across all six of its main campuses, ranging from traditional dormitories to modern self-catered apartments.</p><p>Living on campus comes with big benefits, from 24/7 security and supportive residential leaders to fully furnished rooms with Wi‑Fi, utilities, and cleaning included. Plus, most first‑year international students are guaranteed a room if they apply by the deadlines.</p><p style=\"text-align:center;\"><i>If you’re looking for budget-friendly accommodation options outside the campus, feel free to </i><a href=\"https://edvoy.com/app/\"><i><u>download our app</u></i></a><i> and check out the Stays feature!</i></p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<p><strong>1. Library</strong></p><p>You’ll have access to a networked library system featuring a 24-hour Learning Commons at most locations. These spaces offer extensive digital resources, quiet study zones, and computer facilities that you can access around the clock.</p><p><strong>2. Sports</strong></p><p>CSU is well-equipped for active students, offering modern gymnasiums, basketball and tennis courts, and large sporting fields. The university even supports elite athletes with flexible study schedules.</p><p><strong>3. Laboratories</strong></p><p>The university boasts state-of-the-art specialist labs. Depending on your course, you might work in the Science and Engineering labs, Pharmacy and Physiotherapy labs, or even the university's own vineyard and farm used for agricultural research.</p><p><strong>4. Cafeteria</strong></p><p>There are plenty of spots to grab a meal or coffee between classes.<br>&nbsp;</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
